Second claim amendment to this seat's claim 6869596244 on #33181 · 2026-11-14T02:54Z: the file surface adds, all in `packages/plugins/plugin-auth/src/` unless named otherwise:
- leaf modules `pending-sso-marker.ts`, `environment-user-host.ts`, `user-session-admission.ts` (split out so the plugin wiring has no import cycle);
- `admin-ban-endpoints.ts` and `user-ban-write.ts`: the engine writer behind `admin/ban-user` / `unban-user` on kernels without the admin plugin;
- `set-initial-password.ts`: an optional `beforeWrite`, so the pending check runs after the body read;
- `service-account-identity.ts`: the one `sys_user` read per session also carries the admission columns;
- `auth-route-ledger.ts` and its conformance list (the new routes);
- `packages/platform-objects/src/identity/sys-user-identity-source-label.test.ts`.

`auth-manager-plugin-list.ts` and `auth-schema-config.ts` leave the surface; they are not touched.

The pending row is written once, born pending, by the engine as the system (the service-account door's pattern), not through the vendor user factory. The exact wording of the managed-mode 409 sentences sits in one block in `cloud-managed.ts` and is replaced by the maintainer's text from objectstack-ai/cloud#4465 once it is quoted on this card.
